    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is delighted to bring to the market 25 Haddington Road, a handsome and superbly bright and spacious two-storey over garden level home extending to approximately 206 sq. m., (2,218 sq. ft. approx.) built in 1900 and ideally positioned on Haddington Road in the heart of Dublin 4.\n \nWhile in need of modernisation, this substantial property offers generously proportioned accommodation and significant potential for the new owner to create a wonderful contemporary family home.\n \nAt hall floor level the property opens into a welcoming entrance hall, leading to a generous dining room, separate sitting room and a kitchen/breakfast room.\nThe upper accommodation comprises three bedrooms, (main with an en-suite shower room), together with a large family bathroom located on the return.\nThe garden level provides exceptionally versatile additional accommodation, comprising a kitchen/living/dining room, bedroom, shower room, guest w.c, and a useful storeroom/study. This level offers excellent flexibility for family living, guest accommodation, working from home or independent living, subject to any necessary planning permissions.\n\nThe property also comes with the added bonus of having planning permission to extend, heighten and widen the rear of the property that is valid until 2030. Dublin City Council planning reference WEB1335/24.\n \nExternally, there is a nice back garden that is mainly gravelled with some shrubbery and with the added bonus of rear access, while to the front is a small garden, providing an attractive approach to the property. \n \nThe appeal of this impressive home is further enhanced by its exceptionally convenient and historic location within minutes' walk of an excellent range of local shops, restaurants, and schools. Many of Dublin's Commercial Headquarters, including the I.T. Communications hub of South Docklands are also within walking distance."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway: - \nspacious and bright hallway with beautiful, polished timber floor, ceiling coving, centre rose and attractive arch.\n\nDining Room: - \nwith attractive fireplace, polished timber floor, ceiling coving and centre rose.\n\nSitting Room: - \nwith attractive fireplace, polished timber floors, ceiling coving and centre rose. Overlooking the back garden.\n\nKitchen/Breakfast Room: - \nwith built in wall and floor presses, integrated oven, hob and extractor fan. Plumbed for dishwasher and washing machine. Door to the back garden.\n\nGARDEN LEVEL - \n\n\nEntrance - \n\n\nKitchen/Living/Dining room: - \nopen plan area with built in floor presses, oven, hob and extractor fan and plumbed for dishwasher and washing machine.\n\nBedroom 4: - \nsuperb spacious double bedroom with attractive flooring, ceiling coving and centre rose. Overlooking the back garden.\n\nBedroom 5 - \noverlooking the back garden.\n\nGuest w.c.: - \nwith w.c. and wash hand basin.\n\nShower Room: - \nwith shower cubicle, w.c. and wash hand basin.\n\nStorage press. - \n\n\nUPSTAIRS - \n\n\nLanding: - \nspacious and bright landing with Velux window.\n\nBathroom: - \nspacious bathroom with bath, shower, w.c and wash and basin, part tiled walls, tiled floor and panelled ceiling.\n\nMain Bedroom: - \nwith built in wardrobes and polished timber floorboards.\n\nEnsuite Shower Room: - \nwith shower cubicle, w.c. and wash and basin, polished timber floor and part tiled walls.\n\nBedroom 2: - \nwith built in wardrobes and dressing table, attractive fireplace and timber flooring.\n\nBedroom 3: - \nsingle room with built in wardrobe.\n\n"
      },
